35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Only two firms can dig here, and they flagged clay slippage. The south can be hoarded, but the centre can’t.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Most people cross on firm ground to reach the tram. Drainage callouts doubled after the culvert was capped.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,The groundskeeping roll is down to seven. But two volunteer groups are already active on weekends.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The overflow basin is fine, but the civic hall apron has been patched three times. Half the avenue trees died.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Planted ground costs triple to maintain. The habitat fund only pays for planting and water, not buildings.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if drainage is failing, water-based plans are risky. But the south can be phased.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, exactly. The heat readings are high too. We need a plan that works with the ground, not against it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Minako, the dead trees worry me. If we plant more, who will water them? The roll is too small.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, you’re right. The aftercare was ignored before. We must avoid plans that need constant specialist care.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the fund terms are strict. No money for surfacing or buildings. We must stick to planting and water.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, that’s a huge constraint. Wetland Restoration fits the fund, but the drainage is already struggling.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the drainage callouts are a red flag. But the wetland plan manages water, it doesn’t just add to it.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But who will maintain the reed beds? The volunteers are already busy with the youth league.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the volunteer group upriver does habitat tasks. They might help with the wetland, but it’s a stretch.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the upkeep cost is high, but the fund covers the capital. The long-term cost is the real risk.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m leaning towards Wetland Restoration. It fits the fund and the phasing, but we must fix the drainage first.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I agree. The wetland plan addresses the drainage issue directly. It’s the only one that works with the site’s reality.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I’m a bit worried about the maintenance, but the volunteers might help. I’ll support the wetland plan.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,The past shows we fail at aftercare. But the wetland plan is the only one the fund supports. I’ll vote for it.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"The cost is high, but the fund covers the start. It’s the only viable option given the constraints. I vote for Wetland Restoration.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
